zebra/dplane_fpm_nl: read the VRF id from rtm_table in route notifications

SONiC's FPM encoding (sonic-frr patch 0008) puts the VRF id into rtm_table.
fpmsyncd echoes each route back with RTM_F_OFFLOAD; read the VRF from the
table field and let zebra look the table up (sonic-frr patch 0026), as
SONiC's dplane_fpm_sonic does. Without this the notification finds no VRF
(table 0) and routes stay "queued", never "offloaded".

diff --git a/zebra/dplane_fpm_nl.c b/zebra/dplane_fpm_nl.c
index 8e12083..2c6b5c4 100644
--- a/zebra/dplane_fpm_nl.c
+++ b/zebra/dplane_fpm_nl.c
@@ -731,17 +731,12 @@ static void fpm_read(struct event *t)
 
 			if (netlink_route_notify_read_ctx(hdr, 0, ctx) >= 0) {
 				/*
-				 * Receiving back a netlink message from
-				 * the fpm.  Currently the netlink messages
-				 * do not have a way to specify the vrf
-				 * so it must be unknown.  I'm looking
-				 * at you sonic.  If you are reading this
-				 * and wondering why it's not working
-				 * you must extend your patch to translate
-				 * the tableid to the vrfid and set the
-				 * tableid to 0 in order for this to work.
+				 * SONiC: with the FPM encoding of patch 0008
+				 * rtm_table carries the VRF id (0 = default),
+				 * as dplane_fpm_sonic reads it back.
 				 */
-				dplane_ctx_set_vrf(ctx, VRF_UNKNOWN);
+				dplane_ctx_set_vrf(ctx, dplane_ctx_get_table(ctx));
+				dplane_ctx_set_table(ctx, ZEBRA_ROUTE_TABLE_UNKNOWN);
 				/* Add to the list for batching */
 				dplane_ctx_enqueue_tail(&batch_list, ctx);
 			} else {
